## What it does

```
raw overdue loan ─► feature engineering ─► KMeans segment distances ─► calibrated classifier ─► P(loss)
                                                                                                   │
                     risk band ◄── value-optimised threshold ◄─────────────────────────────────────┘
                         │
                         ▼
   playbook (affordability × collateral × exposure) ─► action · expected loss · priority rank · risk flags
```

| Risk band | Condition | Action |
|---|---|---|
| Low | – | **Automated Reminder**: SMS/app nudges, allow self-cure |
| Medium | EMI ≥ 50% of income | **EMI Restructuring**: tenure extension / lower EMI |
| Medium | otherwise | **Personal Outreach**: agent calls, payment plan |
| High | collateral covers dues | **Collateral Enforcement**: legal notice + asset recovery |
| High | under-secured, outstanding ≥ ₹5 L | **Settlement Negotiation**: one-time settlement + legal notice |
| High | under-secured, small exposure | **Agency Referral & Provisioning** |

Every loan also gets:
- **Expected loss** = outstanding × P(loss) × LGD, where LGD accounts for collateral after a 30% haircut (for provisioning)
- **Net escalation value** = P(loss) × uplift × outstanding − escalation cost (for ordering the work queue)
- **Risk flags**: plain-language reasons such as "Severely overdue (180+ days past due)"

